Haakon Studebaker wrote:

> But why wouldn't a nymph's magical inventory be nullified by a wand of 
> cancellation?

Because monsters count as containers. If you zap a monster, the 
outermost layer (the monster itself and items on the floor) is affected, 
if you zap yourself, everything on the same layer as the wand or further 
outside (yourself, if clay golem, and your inventory, but nothing inside 
bags) is affected. Makes some kind of sense to me. The same kind of 
sense as MR not helping versus self-targeted death rays.

